  "target_audience": "Working software developers (junior to senior), engineering leads, and technical managers who are evaluating or adopting AI tools. They understand code and development workflows but want practical insight on how AI changes their day-to-day work, career trajectory, and team dynamics—not hype or high-level strategy.",
  "sections": [
    {
      "section_type": "introduction",
      "description": "Open with a concrete scenario showing a developer's workflow with AI today vs. two years ago. State the thesis: AI isn't just autocomplete—it's reshaping how code is written, reviewed, tested, and maintained. Preview the article's arc: current tools → workflow changes → skill shifts → organizational impact → future outlook.",
      "style_guide": "Technical but accessible. Lead with a relatable vignette, not abstraction. Avoid marketing language. Use 'we' to align with practitioner perspective. ~150 words.",
      "target_length": 150
    },
